 ## Ownership boundaries
 
-### Theme
+### Theme: `mba-menuiseries`
+
+Presentation only: templates, patterns, design tokens, responsive layout primitives, navigation presentation, and reusable visual treatments. Theme changes must not define or delete business content types/fields.
+
+### Site Core plugin: `mba-site-core`
 
-The theme owns presentation: templates, patterns, styles, navigation presentation, and reusable visual components.
+Durable business behavior: post types, taxonomies, metadata, validation, bidirectional relationships, admin editing UI, global settings, launch checks, and later form behavior. Products/projects remain registered when a different theme is activated.
 
-### Site Core plugin
+### Responsive design baseline
 
-The plugin owns durable business data: content types, taxonomies, metadata, validation, relationships, global settings, and future form integration.
+The theme is mobile-first: 360 px and 390 px use the single-column baseline; 430 px enables two-column primitives where appropriate; 768 px introduces split/three-column layouts; 1024 px enables four-column grids; and 1440 px increases section breathing room within the 1240 px wide-content limit. Components use fluid type/spacing and avoid fixed content heights so 200% text zoom can reflow instead of clipping.
 
 ### Media
 
-WordPress Media Library stores originals. Templates use featured images and galleries chosen by editors. Future media work must add upload guidance, responsive formats, crop rules, and performance safeguards without preventing the owner from replacing photographs.
+WordPress Media Library owns images/documents. Product cover images use the core featured-image field; galleries store attachment IDs in editor-defined order; finish swatches may reference image attachments; technical documents store a validated PDF attachment ID. Templates must tolerate missing media and use normal WordPress responsive image APIs so portrait and landscape owner uploads can be cropped/presented safely.
+
+No ALUMED images are bundled in this batch. `docs/sample-media-sources.md` defines provenance rules and the plugin exposes a Site Health launch check for any content marked temporary.
+
+## Persistence and ownership
+
+Compose uses two named volumes:
+
+- `database_data`: MariaDB data, including all posts/meta/settings.
+- `wordpress_data`: the generated WordPress installation and uploads.
+
+The custom theme/plugin directories are bind-mounted from the repository. `docker compose down` preserves named volumes; `./bin/reset.sh --yes` intentionally deletes them. The CLI service runs as UID/GID 33 (`www-data`) to avoid creating root-owned WordPress files in the shared volume.
+
+## Supported runtime
+
+- Local reference runtime: WordPress 7.1.0, PHP 8.3, MariaDB 11.4.13.
+- Custom PHP compatibility floor: PHP 8.1.
+- Plugin WordPress floor: WordPress 7.0.
 
+Production should run a currently supported WordPress security release and PHP version after staging verification; version changes must be reviewed as explicit dependency updates rather than silently floating Docker tags.
