+# Sample media sources
+
+No third-party photographs are bundled in this patch. In particular, no ALUMED image is copied or hotlinked by the theme/plugin.
+
+The MBA owner has stated that ALUMED photographs may be used temporarily for local/staging development. If a later seed/import step uses that permission, every downloaded file must be stored as replaceable WordPress media and this document must record:
+
+| Local filename / attachment | Exact ALUMED source page | Exact image URL | Retrieved | Permission/purpose | Launch status |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| _None in this batch_ | — | — | — | — | — |
+
+Rules for future temporary media:
+
+- Only `alumed.tn` photographs may use the stated temporary permission.
+- Never hotlink; download, optimize to WebP where appropriate, and import to the Media Library.
+- Never represent an ALUMED project photograph as an MBA realization.
+- Do not copy ALUMED company copy, claims, certifications, testimonials, contact data, or statistics.
+- Mark any seeded product/project with `mba_sample_content = 1` and each temporary Media Library attachment with `mba_temporary_media_source` so **Tools → Site Health** reports a critical launch warning until it is replaced or removed.
+- If exact provenance cannot be recorded, use a neutral locally generated placeholder for testing instead of guessing.
